{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 ./.trellis/scripts/get_context.py --mode phase --step 1.4 --platform codex\nsed -n '1,220p' .trellis/tasks/09-20-ipv6-server-name-run/prd.md\"","aggregated_output":"#### 1.4 Activate task `[required · once]`\n\nAfter artifact review, flip the task status to `in_progress`:\n\n```bash\npython3 ./.trellis/scripts/task.py start <task-dir>\n```\n\nFor lightweight tasks, `prd.md` can be enough. For complex tasks, `prd.md`, `design.md`, and `implement.md` must exist and be reviewed before start. On sub-agent-dispatch platforms, `implement.jsonl` and `check.jsonl` must both have real curated entries before start. Runtime consumers tolerate missing or seed-only manifests for compatibility, but that tolerance is not a planning-ready state.\n\nAfter this command succeeds, the breadcrumb auto-switches to `[workflow-state:in_progress]`, and the rest of Phase 2 / 3 follows.\n\nIf `task.py start` errors with a session-identity message (no context key from hook input, `TRELLIS_CONTEXT_ID`, or platform-native session env), follow the hint in the error to set up session identity, then retry.\n# Fix IPv6 SERVER_NAME development-server fallback\n\n## Goal\n\nAllow ``Flask.run()`` to derive the correct development-server address from a\nbracketed IPv6 ``SERVER_NAME`` value.\n\n## Confirmed Facts\n\n- ``Flask.run`` currently splits ``SERVER_NAME`` at its first colon in\n  ``src/flask/app.py``. This turns ``[::1]:8080`` into host ``[`` and an\n  invalid port fragment.\n- ``tests/test_basic.py::test_run_from_config`` covers the same fallback\n  behavior, including an explicitly supplied port of ``0``.\n\n## Requirements\n\n- When no host or port is supplied to ``app.run()``,\n  ``SERVER_NAME=\"[::1]:8080\"`` must call the development server with host\n  ``\"::1\"`` and port ``8080``.\n- Existing hostname-and-port behavior and explicitly supplied port ``0``\n  behavior must remain unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A regression case in ``test_run_from_config`` asserts that\n  ``[::1]:8080`` derives host ``::1`` and port ``8080``.\n- [ ] The existing hostname and port-zero parameter cases continue to pass.\n- [ ] The provisioned public test command passes.\n\n## Out of Scope\n\n- Changes to URL routing, URL generation, request handling, or the Flask CLI.\n- Validation or normalization of arbitrary malformed ``SERVER_NAME`` values.\n\n## Key Decision\n\n- Keep parsing local to ``Flask.run`` because this fallback is the only\n  affected consumer. Do not introduce a shared parser for one small,\n  configuration-specific split.\n\n## Open Questions\n\nNone. The requested behavior and compatibility constraints are complete.\n\n## Notes\n\nThis is a lightweight task; a PRD is sufficient.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
